WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.990
Drone-based inspection improves access, documentation, repeatability,

00:00:02.990 --> 00:00:05.399
and safety when properly planned.

00:00:05.399 --> 00:00:10.697
It supports roofs, bridges, towers, utilities, solar arrays, corridors, industrial sites,

00:00:10.697 --> 00:00:12.624
facilities, and damage assessment.

00:00:12.624 --> 00:00:17.923
Begin with a bounded inspection question, asset, required detail, constraints, deliverables,

00:00:17.923 --> 00:00:19.849
specialist needs, and exclusions.

00:00:19.849 --> 00:00:24.666
Plan current rules, permissions, weather, obstacles, standoff, route, crew communication,

00:00:24.666 --> 00:00:27.075
battery segments, and emergency options.

00:00:27.075 --> 00:00:30.446
Select R G B, zoom, thermal, video,

00:00:30.446 --> 00:00:34.782
or specialized sensors according to evidence needs and limitations.

00:00:34.782 --> 00:00:40.080
Capture stable overview, intermediate, and close-up views with coverage, scale context,

00:00:40.080 --> 00:00:42.007
metadata, and repeatable routes.

00:00:42.007 --> 00:00:47.306
Organize originals, notes, tags, maps, and reports with traceable evidence references.

00:00:47.306 --> 00:00:51.641
Protect sensitive infrastructure data and state confidence, collection limits,

00:00:51.641 --> 00:00:55.013
missing coverage, and need for qualified interpretation.

00:00:55.013 --> 00:00:57.903
The goal is useful inspection support,

00:00:57.903 --> 00:01:01.756
not replacing engineering judgment or forcing unsafe missions.

00:01:01.756 --> 00:01:06.573
Strong programs combine safe flight, disciplined capture, defensible evidence, privacy,

00:01:06.573 --> 00:01:08.500
security, and specialist review.
